ryonic development or do they come  later during adult development  and to do this we used a tool called the  ms4a3  lineage tracing and this was published  last year  and it is a really great tool uh because  linux tracing and macrophages used to be  quite difficult um but this mass  using ms403 td tomato lineage tracing  labels all adult bone marrow drive  macrocharges  because it's active in the progenitor of  the adult macrophages but not the  embryonic macrophages  so what you see here is that at birth  there are no macrophages labeled because  they're all embryonic  then during growth  populations such as microglia which are  embryonic for life  are not contributed to at all by adult  bone marrow macrophages  whereas other populations such as  the colon and the small intestine are  quickly replaced by adult macrophages as  the mysql  and so when we looked at the frequency  of the mass providers in early  mammary gland development this is during  puberty here from four to six weeks  you get a really rapid increase in  industrial macrophages  whereas the other populations are more  steady in this time  and then looking at these my switch  tracks  the adult macrophages before puberty  only a few of them are adult derived so  most of them are embryonic  but then during this ductile growth an  increase in numbers in dms  they're coming in from the bone marrow  and then this stabilizes more as they  grow older  so initially ductile macrophages are  embryonic but and  as the guts grow and branch during  puberty  they come in from the bone marrow  and then to get more of an idea of  what these cells might be doing we did  rna sequencing  and this showed using this mds plot here  that the duster microphotos are really  different  from the other myeloid cells in the  mammary gland  and they have a signature of phagocytic  enzymes and also when we compare the  doctor microphotos to the other  macrophages  we brought out this not signaling  signature which is interesting 